On Oct 23, 2017, at 2:12 PM, Ackermann, Michael <MAckermann@bcbsm.com> =
wrote:
> To suggest that I or my industry does not take security seriously, is =
inaccurate and immaterial to this discussion.=20

I'm sure you take security seriously.   What I'm saying is that you have =
tunnel vision about it, because you are caught between a rock (the IETF) =
and a hard place (management that won't listen).
=20
> I would put the comment  that anyone or any industry is attempting to =
lay costs for anything off on IETF,  in the same unfortunate bucket.=20

By "we" I mean users of the Internet, not the IETF.  The IETF doesn't =
have deep pockets.
=20
> These types of subjectively negative statements are not at all =
constructive, germane nor worthy of response.


That's fine.   We would all like for this conversation to end.   My =
"subjectively negative statements" were just explaining to you why you =
aren't making any headway in the working group in trying to get the =
outcome you seek.


--Apple-Mail=_29DC32DF-1AF1-4239-A16F-E2DD30DFE619
